HbTK

HbTK was pulled from the Hackedbox source to separate its GUI structure
from the main window manager.

The purpose is to retain the classic Hackedbox look and feel associated
with the early 2000s while bringing the GUI structure forward for modern
development.

The original Hackedbox interface was procedurally constructed. HbTK
continues that approach rather than replacing the interface with an
image-based theme system.

HbTK will provide the foundation for developing and extending the
Hackedbox GUI while preserving its original character.